---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About · phi" description="About this site.">
  <article class="post-content">
    <p class="post-meta">About</p>
    <h1 class="post-title">About this site</h1>
    <p class="post-subtitle">A small library of long-form essays.</p>

    <p>
      This is a personal notebook of essays on the history of religion, the
      philosophy of violence, and the long arc by which ideas turn into their
      opposites. The pieces here are written to be read slowly — paragraph by
      paragraph — rather than skimmed.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where it helps, the essays come with a companion audio version. The
      audio is a two-voice spoken dialog, synthesized locally on Apple Silicon
      with the open-source <a href="https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M">Kokoro</a> text-to-speech model running through MLX.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed
      on <a href="https://vercel.com">Vercel</a>, and styled in plain CSS.
      Body text is set in <em>Crimson Pro</em>; the small caps and metadata
      use <em>Inter</em>. The cover artwork was generated with OpenAI's
      <em>gpt-image-2</em>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
